BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Our Safe Space Training is an intensive\, interactive training
  that provides attendees with information and tools to combat homophobia\
 , biphobia\, transphobia\, cissexism and heterosexism\, on campus and bey
 ond. Through interactive activities and discussion\, participants will pe
 rsonally reflect on their own experiences to enhance their personal and p
 rofessional development\, provide further education\, and finally\, ident
 ify ways to create change on campus and beyond.\nAll sessions are three h
 ours and are first-come\, first-served. Pre-registration is required. Reg
 istrants are expected to attend the full session. Only individuals who ha
 ve fully completed the Safe Space Program and have agreed to the expectat
 ions of its membership are able to display the sticker/button of our prog
 ram. Refreshments are not provided\; however\, you are more than welcome 
 to bring your lunch\, coffee\, snacks\, etc.\n\nHosted by: Advocacy and O
 utreach\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.camp
 uslabs.com/engage/event/11332857
DTEND:20260616T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260531T042730Z
DTSTART:20260616T170000Z
LOCATION:Cole Hall 141
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
